this is a second thought video in  collaboration with Kento bento make sure  to check out their video after this for  years society has been obsessed with the  idea of some far-off point when the  future begins usually involving flying  cars or spaceships or super intelligent  robots regardless of when we think this  bright and shiny future will arrive in  all its glory it's exciting to try to  predict upcoming events especially those  within our lifetime but there are so  many possible future events around the  world that we'd never be able to cover  the most interesting ones so without  further ado let's take a look at a few  of the projected events in North America  by the middle of the century just around  the corner in early to mid 2019 we'll  get to witness one of the most highly  anticipated space launches in recent  memory the James Webb Space Telescope  originally slated for launch in October  of 2018 will finally begin its  operations in space giving us new  insights into the early universe capable  of seeing the very first generation of  stars that form just 200 million years  after the Big Bang Webb's four main  objectives are to study the formation  and evolution of galaxies search for  light from the first stars and galaxies  that formed after the Big Bang  understand the formation of stars and  planetary systems and to study these  planetary systems and the origins of  life the launch of the James Webb Space  Telescope will mark the beginning of a  very exciting time for space exploration  in 2020 we'll see the first test flights  of NASA's quiet supersonic technology  their new low boom supersonic passenger  planes will be a departure from  traditional tube and wing airplane  construction and are intended to make  air travel greener safer and quieter  reducing fossil fuel use emissions and  noise the new technologies employed by  these planes will lead to a savings of  approximately 255 billion dollars  between 2025 and 2050 also in 2020  Glacier National Park in Montana will  have become completely ice-free the  parks namesake having disappeared as a  result of global warming and earlier  prediction for this event put the  estimate at 2030 but more recent data  gathered in 2009 has indicated a  temperature increase more than twice as  rapid as previously thought many cold  water dependent plants and animals will  die off including a number of rare  species the lack of spring melt will  decrease the overall water level in the  area and lead to more frequent and  severe wildfires finally 2020 we'll also  see a drastically increased number of  drone  patrolling the skies of the United  States in 2012 there were about 7,000  drones used mainly for counter-narcotics  applications and public relief efforts  by 2020 we'll see a fleet of official  drone sporting advanced monitoring  equipment including infrared cameras and  radar and some models will even be  equipped with tasers and rubber bullets  in some cities these drones will be used  to monitor protests and spy on citizens  with no warrant or legal process  needless to say these plans have raised  some very serious privacy and civil  liberty concerns in 2023 NASA will  launch the first manned test flight of  its Orion spacecraft the vessel that  will eventually take humans to Mars four  astronauts will be carried to a distant  orbit about 71 thousand kilometres from  the moon for about two weeks this  mission will be the first time humans  have left low-earth orbit since Apollo  17 in December of 1972 more than 50  years earlier on April 8th 2024 North  America will experience a total solar  eclipse it will be the first total solar  eclipse visible from the US since 2017  the first visible from Mexico since 1991  and the first visible from Canada since  1979 it will be the only total solar  eclipse of the 21st century where  totality is visible from all three  countries in 2025 will potentially see  another amazing spacecraft make its  debut the advanced technology large  aperture Space Telescope or at last will  dwarf not only Hubble but also the James  Webb Space Telescope with a 16 metre  primary mirror versus 6.5 meters on Webb  at last will be designed to search for  life in the galaxy detecting bio  signatures such as oxygen and water the  craft will have such a powerful  resolution that it'll be able to detect  the composition of atmospheres and the  ground conditions of exoplanets up to a  hundred and fifty light years away by  2028 scientists expect to have brought  several extinct species back to life  back in 2009 the first successful  de-extinction lasted just seven minutes  after a Pyrenean ibex was born and  quickly succumbed to lung defects the  species most likely to be brought back  include the wild pigeon and the dodo by  the end of the 2020s any hope of  recovering the titanic will have faded  decades under the water and exposure to  metal eating bacteria will have reduced  the once-mighty vessel to an  insignificant rust  however some artifacts on board may  remain in a recoverable State by the  beginning of the 2030s many experts  expect the United States to be declining  as a world power growing national debt  drastically reduced manufacturing and an  over stretched military are expected to  weaken the US economy significantly  allowing other nations a chance to grab  some of the global spotlight we may see  Shanghai eclipse Wall Street as the  leading financial center and China and  India are expected to make a huge impact  on the world stage the US will maintain  its superpower status but will probably  be less of the behemoth it once was by  the latter half of the 2030s we could  likely see permanent manned bases on the  moon made possible partly by the  development of new heavy-lift rockets  it's expected that NASA other foreign  space agencies as well as private  organizations will be researching and  constructing human habitats both  independently and in cooperation with  foreign and domestic partners by 2037  the number of bombers in the US Air  Force will have fallen below the  required 170 aircraft due to a number of  reasons including the decommissioning of  the last b-52s currently given the  clever codename 2037 bomber this new  generation stealth bomber will  supposedly be the most advanced aircraft  ever created equipped with unparalleled  stealth technology a range that enables  it to strike targets almost anywhere in  the world a payload which includes  nuclear capability and the option to be  piloted remotely or even completely  autonomously during the early 2040 we'll  likely see a submarine mission to  Saturn's moon Titan NASA will deliver an  unmanned submarine probe to one of the  huge methane lakes on Titan and the  craft will gather critical data and  high-definition video of the strange  subsurface world this environment  couldn't support life as we know it on  earth but that doesn't mean we won't  discover something a little more alien  also during the early to mid 20 40 s  we'll probably see the last World War  two veterans pass away marking the end  of first-hand accounts of what will  probably be the last global scale war  some of these veterans may live to see  the hundredth anniversary commemoration  of d-day On June 6 2014 the state a time  capsule will be opened close to Normandy  which contains newspaper articles and  letters from the time including a  message from President Eisenhower to  future generations by the end of the  2040s many Gulf Coast cities will have  to be abandoned due to the  ongoing threat of super hurricanes  climate change will have sparked the  emergence of these unbelievably powerful  storms leading to the temporary and  sometimes permanent evacuation of  coastal cities 200 mile per hour winds  flash floods and waves dozens of meters  high overwhelm cities like Houston and  New Orleans causing untold devastation  and finally by 2050 we should see a  world more connected than ever before  at this point practically all major  continents with the exception of poor  lonely Australia will be connected to  each other by highway rail or tunnel  interestingly the pan-american highway  was just barely disconnected until this  point the massive highway that stretches  all the way from Prudhoe Bay in Alaska  down to via Argentina is only broken by  a 106 kilometers called the Darien Gap a  giant stretch of untamed swamp and  forest impossible to cross by  conventional motor vehicle once a road  across the Darien Gap can be established  the world will essentially be completely  connected by ground-based transportation  if you're interested to learn more about  the trans global highways that relates  to Asia and some of the exciting  upcoming events in that region of the  world make sure to watch this video by  Kento bento next these are just a small  selection of the likely events leading  up to the middle of the century and who  knows what other surprises we have in  store the future might not be all flying  cars and robots but we certainly have  some exciting and terrifying things to  look forward to thanks for watching and  we'll see you next week

